**FINDINGS.** Startup works on the current `dist/`, but a few checks weren't done, so I can't mark it PASS.

- **Build and server:** port 8000 was free. `make` had nothing to rebuild, and `web/` matches `dist/`. I started a `python3 -m http.server` on 8000 and stopped it afterwards.
- **Loading:** a fresh Playwright load returned 200 for the page and all six assets (`doom.js`, `doom.wasm`, `doom.data` and three helper scripts). The console showed 0 errors.
- **Canvas:** 640x400, shown at 1152x720 with the aspect ratio kept.
- **Frame loop:** the frame counter went from 317 to 365 in one second, so it is running.
- **Image:** the screenshot shows the attract-demo gameplay with HUD and correct colours, no corruption.

**One minor warning:** the console shows two "AudioContext was not allowed to start" warnings before any user gesture (`audio_web.js:27` and `:53`). That is expected from browser autoplay rules. The owner is `coder_input_audio`, and checking audio after a gesture is left to `reviewer_gameplay`.

**Not verified:**
- exact time to first frame
- a clean rebuild
- other browsers and viewport sizes
- warm-cache reload
- audio after a gesture

I assumed headless Chromium and chose my own pass criteria, since no spec was supplied. The report is at `artifacts/logs/reviewer_site.FnUrtZ/report.md`, with `startup.png`, `console.txt` and `server.log` beside it.